WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(dramatic music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.440
- In a world of quarantine

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.560
where no one is allowed outside

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.900
and the only way to connect
online is through the internet.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.260
- [Nicole] This is Jon Bailey,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.250
a professional voiceover artist.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.810
You may also know him as

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.220
- My name is Optimus Prime.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.680
Autobots, transform and roll out.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.600
And I fill out quite a few
times for Mister Ryan Reynolds,

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.950
depending on what he's in the mood for.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.760
You know, what color pants he's wearing.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.080
I've also filled in for Chris
Hemsworth quite a few times

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.150
and most recently Leonardo DiCaprio

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.070
in Once Upon a Time in Hollywood.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.610
- But really he has actually

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:38.810
subbed in for them in trailers and movies.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.330
Clearly, we're not all voiceover
artists with fancy setups,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.130
but we are trying to sound our best

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.970
whether it's on a phone
call, or a Zoom call.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.810
Even Jon here doesn't
sound perfect over Zoom

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.360
without his fancy
whisper room sound booth.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.650
How's it going?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:54.483
- It's pretty good.

00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:56.252
Just stuck inside like everybody else.

00:00:56.252 --> 00:00:57.085
(laughing)

00:00:57.085 --> 00:00:57.918
- Nice.

00:00:57.918 --> 00:00:59.443
- You want me to call back from booth

00:00:59.443 --> 00:01:01.043
so I can get better audio?

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.490
- [Nicole] So I asked Jon to share

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.630
the best ways we can
sound better from home.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.250
He had three big tips.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.720
- All right, does that sound better?

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.610
- [Nicole] Number one: your environment.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.280
- [Jon] You don't want
sound to bounce around.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.600
The environment you're in right now,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.591
you're hearing a lot of this room echo.

00:01:16.591 --> 00:01:18.280
- [Nicole] Hello, hello!

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.200
Echo!

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.510
Do you hear me?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:22.330
- [Jon] Where in my booth
you don't hear that anymore

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.150
because the sound absorbs into it.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.660
- [Nicole] Jon's best advice:

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.410
get some moving blankets.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.120
- [Jon] Some super
professional voice actors,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.330
they don't even have a fancy booth.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.460
They're just using moving blankets

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.290
from the hardware store down the street.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.425
- The takeaway: hard flat surfaces

00:01:35.425 --> 00:01:38.130
like these are your enemy.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.800
You could get fancy acoustic foam

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.280
to hang on your walls like
the kind that Jon has,

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.830
but choosing a room with
a lot of soft stuff,

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.600
rugs, couches, things
hanging on the walls,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.130
will get you close.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.600
Number two: your microphone.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.254
When it comes to your
microphone, size matters.

00:01:54.254 --> 00:01:56.990
The part of the microphone
that captures your voice

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.440
is called a capsule.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.660
The bigger the capsule,
the better the sound.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.740
I've been doing some testing

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.370
and if you're looking for
something better than your earbuds

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.900
try this one.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.710
Sure, it's not as good as
Jon's $1000 professional mic,

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.308
but the $130 Blue Yeti does a great job

00:02:12.308 --> 00:02:15.780
at producing warm, clear
audio for video calls.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.670
It's not a solution for phone
calls on your smartphone.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.540
It's best if you're at your computer.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.230
It works with a Mac or PC

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:24.350
and it's mic is pretty much plug and play,

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.860
though there are some knobs on the back

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.700
you need to know about.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.300
- You can actually flip it on to a setting

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.760
that's more built for voice only,

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.110
as opposed to picking up other stuff.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.070
- Is it this one?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.330
- Yeah, that's the one.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:37.570
- If you work in a large
echo-y room like me,

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.370
you can also turn the gain dial down

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.700
to reduce some of that
environmental noise.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.320
There is one important no button
trick to remember, though.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.240
- That is all you have to do.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.060
You make a Y shape, bro, all right,

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.310
hang 10, take your 10 and
put your pinky at the mic

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.520
and your thumb at your mouth.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.310
That's how far away from
the mic you should be.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.630
- Yes, if you have a
high-quality microphone,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.870
maintaining that hang loose
distance is very important,

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:01.460
but for smaller microphones,

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:02.870
you'll tend to get better audio

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.550
if it's closer to your mouth.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.260
That's why for important calls,

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.800
I prefer a headset like this,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.240
call center style.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.780
This one is the Logitech Zone Wireless,

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.460
which has a little arm that
holds out the microphone.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.880
Number three: your connection.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.690
Connection is obviously very important.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.470
You know if you have a
great set up, great mic,

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.700
it doesn't matter if you
have a shoddy connection.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.743
- That's 100% true.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.790
- Slow internet speeds
or a bad wifi signal

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.660
can make you sound terrible,

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.790
so for video calls, a wired connection

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.290
over an ethernet cable is best.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.800
But if that's not an option,

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.500
sitting close to your router can also

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.540
improve the strength of your connection.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.670
You can also turn off your video

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.540
to save that bandwidth for audio.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.100
The service you choose also matters.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.790
For instance, the Zoom
video conferencing app

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.440
automatically suppresses
background noise and echo.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.000
Test your mic in the app's audio settings,

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.310
then click on advanced
to turn up the feature

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.280
to aggressive or off.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.060
Lastly, using a wired
headset like this one

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.090
can eliminate any Bluetooth
or interference issues.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.500
And while all of these tips
should help you sound better,

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.790
they probably can't
transform you into Jon.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.240
- Rated PG 13, starts Friday
in theaters everywhere,

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.253
except that the theaters are closed.

